<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices up on demand from processors.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices up on demand from processors.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices ended Tuesday up on good demand from processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said prices rose 100-200 rupees per tonne in market and plant delivery condition in active trade and the undertone was firm.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was down 100 rupees per tonne on limited demand from vanaspati units and refineries while soyoil refined was steady, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapesed extraction prices were steady in thin trade with soymeal yellow was $249 to 250 per tonne FAS (free alongside ship) west Indian ports for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $90-91 per tonne FAS (free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3100-3150 rupees per tonne in FOR (free on rail) condition.</p>
<p>Trade was dull and the undertone steady, dealers said.</p>
